# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# 3D sketches in the shared Qt UI on macOS (mitcad#1524-#1527, #1544,
# #1548-#1550): the main steps of tools/ui-sketch3d-test.sh (Linux) and
# tools/ui-windows-sketch3d-test.ps1 (Windows) on sketch3d.json's design:
# Box1 (F1.b0) 40 x 30 x 20 at (20, 20); 3DSketch1 (F2) on its top face with
# the line AB (c3, p1 to p2), a tangent arc (c6), a fit-point spline that
# leaves the face (c9), a reference curve of an upright edge (c10) and a
# closed triangle (p11, p12, p14; c13, c15, c16); Sketch1 (F3), planar.
#   - Create Sketch: 2D by default, 3D on the card; an empty 2D sketch on
#     YZ; an empty new 3D sketch on XZ taken back by Finish.
#   - Edit 3DSketch1: its frame on the face, p2 and the reference curve
#     described in the 3D Sketch Palette, Esc stays in the sketch, Delete of
#     a triangle line; Finish as one undo step, undone. The light bulb.
#   - The drawing tools in a new 3D sketch on XZ: Line by typed offsets and
#     by Axis and Length, Esc layers, Undo; a Fit Point Spline; a Tangent
#     Arc with Radius and Arc Length typed; a Center Point Arc's normal
#     picked from AB; a Point; a Line whose end snaps On Face; Finish.
#   - Editing 3DSketch1: AB's length typed, driven, removed; B dragged along
#     X; a Length added from the palette (a dimension), Fix and Unfix; Delete
#     with Dependents; Replace Reference's pick ended by Esc; Finish.
#   - Sketch1 to a 3D sketch from the Browser's menu and back to 2D by the
#     3D Sketch Palette's box, each one undo step; Convert to 2D Sketch
#     offered on the 3D sketch's row; fully constrained.
#   - Fillet of the triangle's corner p12 with Radius 3 typed.
#   - Plane-bound tools in a new 3D sketch on XY: 2-Point Rectangle from the
#     origin (Width 30, Height 20), undone and redone; Center Diameter
#     Circle on the YZ plane (Radius 8).
#   - Rib from 3DSketch1's curves: the spline out of the sketch plane
#     refused, saying why, the line AB taken; Esc.
#   - Ellipse (10, 5), Circumscribed Polygon (Radius 20) and Text in a
#     dragged frame ("MitCad") in another 3D sketch on XY.
#   - The layout of mitcad#1592: the relation and dimension buttons whole
#     across the card, the selected point's description in its sight, the
#     On Face badge inside the view, one In plane badge for the converted
#     rectangle, the 3D Sketch box disabled while Text runs and enabled as
#     it ends, and the Home view kept by Finish of the converted sketch.
# The tools start by their commands, as in sketch3d-202.mitcad-ui (a key
# goes to the field that has the keyboard). Places in the view are
# percentages of it, near where the Linux test clicks free places; the
# ellipse's and the polygon's sizes go toward the pointer, moved off the
# origin first (to the left, as on Linux); the Text frame is dragged up and
# left of the middle, as on Linux. No drag cancelled by Esc and no tangent handle
# (they need the pointer held while a key goes, or a step only when the
# handle shows); the fillet's radius is typed, as on Windows.
# Run by tools/ui-macos-sketch3d-test.sh.
expect-ever 'View area'
wait-idle
command view.fit
wait-idle
expect-ever '^Browser Root/Sketches/3DSketch1 at '
expect-ever '^Browser sketch DOF: .*3DSketch1 [0-9]+'
expect-ever '^Sketches shown: .*F2'

# Create Sketch: the kind before the plane, 2D by default.
mark
command sketch.create
wait-log '^Create Sketch kind: 2D$'
wait-log '^View banner: Create Sketch: pick a plane'
wait-log '^Create Sketch kind 3D at '
wait-idle
mark
click-logged '^Create Sketch kind 3D at '
wait-log '^Create Sketch kind: 3D$'
wait-log '^View banner: Create 3D Sketch: pick a plane'
mark
click-logged '^Create Sketch kind 2D at '
wait-log '^Create Sketch kind: 2D$'
mark
key Escape
wait-log 'Create Sketch cancelled'
mark
command sketch.create
wait-log '^Create Sketch kind: 2D$'
wait-log '^Datum yz at '
wait-idle
click-logged '^Datum yz at '
wait-log '^Sketch started on yz'
wait-idle
mark
command sketch.finish
wait-log '^Sketch finished'

# Create Sketch with 3D: an empty new 3D sketch, taken back by Finish.
